                     ADAPTED across the library, one statement: the
                     inclusive-design-skills copy of
                     inclusive-interaction/skills/touch-target-design/SKILL.md
                     states the touch minimum as `44x44 CSS pixels (WCAG 2.2
                     Level AA)`. WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) is
                     Level AA at 24x24 CSS px and SC 2.5.5 Target Size
                     (Enhanced) is Level AAA at 44x44, and tezgah's own checker
                     enforces 24 (bin/tezgah-design, `TAP_TARGET`); the adopted
                     copy states 24x24 as the AA floor with its success
                     criterion and keeps 44x44 as the AAA floor and the common
                     platform guideline. Every other adopted byte is upstream's,
                     and `skills/design-library/SOURCE` records the per-file
                     sha256 and names both departures.
                     `skills/design-library/SKILL.md`, `INDEX.md` and `EVALS.md`
                     are tezgah's own files and are not part of the manifest.
